<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">death</ansi>

When your hitpoints fall to zero or less, you'll drop to the ground and begin
to bleed out. While bleeding out, each round you'll fall more and more into 
the negative range. Someone can still heal you back up.

Once you reach -10 hitpoints, you will die!

Dying costs you <ansi fg="yellow">one level</ansi> (at level 1 you keep your level but lose its
progress). Earning that level back doesn't give its training points again.
You may also drop some of your gear, which you'll need to go back for.

You wake at the church of the last city you visited, with your living
companions beside you. Any journey, camp, or inn stay is left behind.
You wake without your wounds (<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>).

Your companions can die too: see <ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>.
